<title>CHINA: ABN Amro HK branch places HK$390 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>ABN Amro HK branch places HK$390 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN Amro Bank's Hong Kong branch has lodged a HK$390 million floating rate certificates of deposit issue due 2000 with the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) Central Moneymarkets Unit.</p>
<p>The three-year certificates were issued at par to float at 21 basis points over the one-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>The minimum denomination is HK$500,000.</p>
<p>The deal was self-arranged by ABN Amro Bank's Hong Kong branch.</p>
<p>The payment date is July 28.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
